<h2 align="center">Common (vernacular) names applied to California vascular plants</h2>
<h3 align="center">compiled by Elizabeth Painter</h3>
<h4 align="center">up to date as of May 1, 2016</h4>
<blockquote>
Common names (also referred to as vernacular names) are applied differently at different times and places by different users.  This list is compiled from many sources and is intended to be as comprehensive as possible. It is not intended to indicate which common name is correct or preferred.  Please send comments about this page to Elizabeth Painter (<a href="mailto:paintere&#64;west.net">paintere&#64;west.net</a>).
<br />
</blockquote>
EOP

use BerkeleyDB;

#open(IN,"${data_path}painter_common_out.txt") || die;
 while(<DATA>){
chomp;

($id,$name,$group,$family,$FamilyC,$GenusC,$SpeciesC,$InfraC,$common1,$common2,$common3,$note,$syn,@residue)=split(/\t/);
$TID{$name}=$id;
